# FACT · build the instrument twice — the invent-computing pillar (2026-08-10)

The invent-computing eclipse (seed 42; FoaF · savannah-savane · medley). The pillar that
survived every project, promoted because it generalizes past its paper:

BUILD THE INSTRUMENT TWICE. Two implementations, independent by construction (A and B),
make agreement EVIDENCE and disagreement INFORMATION. The run's one disagreement was real
— 68 = 4 × 17 — and it corrected the paper (v1), which no amount of single-instrument
confidence would have done. Survived all three seeds: FoaF (independent trust paths),
savannah-savane (two independent reads is forensic doctrine), medley (independent
verification before a change lands).

THE NEGATIVE CONTROL RODE ALONG: non-magic givens demonstrably do NOT join the ladder —
the counterexample that makes the positive claim mean anything (the door's own law: a
claim needs a tool that fails it).

TWO HONESTY MOVES from the same verdict, kept for reuse wherever claims overreach:
- RETELLS, NOT IS: a chosen narrative fit is NAMED as chosen, never passed off as forced
  ("the experiment retells C4's origin" — a fit we chose, not a derivation).
- ROLE-FIT vs READINESS split: "C4 is well-shaped for the judge role" PASSES while "C4
  can be the judge now" FAILS — specced, not built. Split the claim, keep both halves.

